{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS5pDrAahBKzeR6nLbnA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Customers can cancel an active order until a shipment is confirmed; cancellation moves the order to CANCELLED status, cancels its CREATED shipments, and is idempotent; rejections with 409 are atomic; a cancelled order cannot have new shipments created.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (`Order.kt:11-16`) has no status field; only orderId, customerId, amount, currency\n- OrderController (`OrderController.kt:15-46`) has POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId}, GET /orders; no cancel endpoint\n- OrderRepository (`OrderRepository.kt:10-27`) stores orders in a ConcurrentHashMap by orderId\n- Shipment entity (`Shipment.kt:9-14`) already has a status field; ShipmentStatus enum has CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED (`Shipment.kt:23-27`)\n- ShipmentController (`ShipmentController.kt:20-56`) creates shipments always in CREATED status; no validation on order status\n- ShipmentRepository (`ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`) stores shipments in ConcurrentHashMap by shipmentId\n- ErrorCode enum (`ApiError.kt:31-37`) has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (`GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29`) catches ApiException and wraps it in ApiError envelope\n- All errors follow the pattern: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }`\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions; they verify both status and error envelope shape\n- Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for in-memory storage and return sorted lists\n- Tests clear() the repository in @BeforeEach\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — must add status field (OrderStatus enum); cannot be avoided\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId; cannot be avoided  \n3. `OrderController.kt` — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint; cannot be avoided\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add method to find shipments by orderId; cannot be avoided\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders; cannot be avoided\n6. `ApiError.kt` — must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code for shipment rejection; cannot be avoided\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel behaviour; cannot be avoided\n\n**Risks:**\n- Data races if cancel and shipment creation happen concurrently; mitigated by in-memory storage and method-level synchronization\n- Order status field must be initialized on all existing orders; all new orders default to ACTIVE\n- ShipmentRepository needs new method; existing findById and existsById on Order by shipmentId is impossible; must find by orderId instead\n- Existing tests might assume orders have no status field in response; need to verify they still pass\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Question: Does the response of GET /orders/{orderId} include the status field in the JSON? The requirement says \"GET /orders/{orderId} reports it.\" Answer: Yes, the Order data class will serialize to JSON with the status field.\n- Question: When cancelling an order, should we update the status to CANCELLED atomically? Answer: Yes, the requirement says \"the cancel is all-or-nothing\" — if any shipment is CONFIRMED, the order stays ACTIVE and nothing changes. This means we must check before modifying anything.\n\nNo stopping points identified. All questions have been answered by re-reading the requirement.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add an `OrderStatus` enum with values ACTIVE, CANCELLED. Add a `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class. Initialize new orders to ACTIVE by default. The CreateOrderRequest does not need a status field; the endpoint always creates with ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add a method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` — wait, this is wrong. We need a way to find shipments for an order. This doesn't belong in OrderRepository. Instead, we add a method to ShipmentRepository called `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for a given order.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add a method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` that returns all shipments with a matching orderId, sorted by shipmentId.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt**: Add a POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint. The method:\n   - Finds the order; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, succeed and return the order unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with a new error code (need to add it)\n   - Mark all CREATED shipments for this order as CANCELLED\n   - Mark the order as CANCELLED\n   - Save and return the order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the create() method, after loading the order (we need to add this), check if the order is CANCELLED. If so, throw ConflictException with a new error code. Only create the shipment if the order is ACTIVE.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_WITH_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` or similar (for the 409 when shipment is CONFIRMED)\n   - `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CREATE_FOR_CANCELLED_ORDER` or similar (for the 409 when order is CANCELLED)\n\n   Actually, re-reading the requirement: \"If any shipment of the order is CONFIRMED, the cancel is rejected with HTTP 409\" and \"Once an order is CANCELLED, creating a shipment for it (`POST /shipments`) is rejected with HTTP 409.\" Both are 409, but the requirement doesn't name specific error codes. Let me check the pattern: ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, ORDER_NOT_FOUND — these are resource-specific. So I might use ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CREATE_CANCELLED_ORDER, or simpler: ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and SHIPMENT_ORDER_CANCELLED. But the requirement says \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" — let me check what error codes already exist and what pattern they follow. Looking at the enum, they are all NOUN_VERB or NOUN_ADJECTIVE. So I'll use ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT for the cancel rejection and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED for the shipment creation rejection. Wait, let me re-read: \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" — this means I should follow the existing pattern. The codes are: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED. The pattern is NOUN_STATE or NOUN_PROBLEM. So I'll add ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - Test: cancel an active order with no shipments → returns 200 with the order in CANCELLED status\n   - Test: cancel an active order with CREATED shipments → returns 200, shipments are now CANCELLED, order is CANCELLED\n   - Test: cancel a CANCELLED order → returns 200, nothing changes (idempotent)\n   - Test: cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409 with error code, order is still ACTIVE, shipment is still CONFIRMED\n   - Test: cancel an order that doesn't exist → returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test:\n   - Test: create a shipment for a CANCELLED order → returns 409 with error code (ORDER_IS_CANCELLED or similar)\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Alternative: Store order status in a separate ShipmentOrder join table. Rejected because: (1) the requirement doesn't call for it; (2) the in-memory repository pattern uses simple data classes; (3) a single field on the Order entity is sufficient.\n- Alternative: Add a cancel method to OrderRepository that handles atomicity. Rejected because: the controller is the right place for business logic and error handling; the repository just does CRUD.\n- Alternative: Have ShipmentController call OrderRepository to check order status. Rejected initially, then reconsidered: yes, we should do this. The OrderController will inject OrderRepository as a dependency. ShipmentController will also inject OrderRepository to check the order exists and is not CANCELLED before creating a shipment. This is dependency injection, a standard pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancelling an active order with created shipments:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderController.cancel() looks up order in OrderRepository; if not found → throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n3. If order.status == CANCELLED → return the order (200)\n4. Query ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) to get all shipments\n5. Check each shipment's status; if any is CONFIRMED → throw ConflictException (409), nothing changes\n6. For each shipment with status CREATED, update to CANCELLED in ShipmentRepository\n7. Update order.status to CANCELLED in OrderRepository\n8. Return the order (200)\n\n*Cancelling a non-existent order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. OrderRepository.findById(orderId) returns null\n3. Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n*Cancelling an order with a confirmed shipment:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n2. Check shipments; find one with CONFIRMED status\n3. Throw ConflictException (409, ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n4. Nothing is modified; order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n\n*Creating a shipment for a cancelled order:*\n1. POST /shipments with orderId pointing to a CANCELLED order\n2. ShipmentController.create() looks up the order in OrderRepository\n3. If order.status == CANCELLED → throw ConflictException (409, ORDER_IS_CANCELLED)\n4. Otherwise, create the shipment (current behaviour)\n\n*Creating a shipment for a non-existent order:*\n1. POST /shipments with a non-existent orderId\n2. Current behaviour: shipment is created (the requirement says \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour\")\n3. So we only reject if the order exists AND is cancelled\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. OrderControllerTest:\n   - `test_cancel_active_order_without_shipments` — verify order transitions to CANCELLED, returns 200 with updated order\n   - `test_cancel_active_order_with_created_shipments` — verify order and shipments both transition to CANCELLED\n   - `test_cancel_already_cancelled_order` — verify idempotency: second cancel succeeds, returns order\n   - `test_cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment` — verify 409 is thrown, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n   - `test_cancel_nonexistent_order` — verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   - `test_newly_created_order_has_active_status` — verify new orders are ACTIVE by default\n   - (verify existing tests still pass)\n\n2. ShipmentControllerTest:\n   - `test_create_shipment_for_cancelled_order` — verify 409 is thrown, shipment is not created\n   - (verify existing tests still pass, especially that creating a shipment for a non-existent order still works)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me now implement the changes:\n\n1. First, update Order.kt to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":21163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"631afbac-f607-4b7d-8484-5ef324dade4f","uuid":"de00a593-9eb5-421c-84d1-73e5442bcc63","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:53:51.166Z","request_id":"req_011CfS5pDPd1MAXqDDG65dN6"}
