{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS5wWh8XhiJZD1KBguqA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` completed with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All baseline tests (4 OrderController + 5 ShipmentController + 3 CustomerController + 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests = 13 tests) still pass\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.cancel(), tested by:\n   - `test_cancels_an_active_order_without_shipments` \n   - `test_cancels_an_active_order_and_cancels_its_CREATED_shipments`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409) with ErrorCode enum values, following existing pattern\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Tested by:\n   - `test_cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_is_idempotent` \n   - `test_cannot_cancel_order_with_a_CONFIRMED_shipment` (verifies atomicity)\n   - `test_cannot_cancel_a_non_existent_order`\n   - `test_rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order`\n   - `test_creates_a_shipment_for_a_non_existent_order` (baseline behaviour preserved)\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — Only modified Kotlin source and test files; no changes to pom.xml\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified files required for the feature:\n   - Order.kt (added OrderStatus enum and status field)\n   - OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository)\n   - OrderRepository.kt — NOT modified (no new methods needed)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method)