1. `Order.kt` — Added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field with default ACTIVE\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Added POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with idempotent semantics, atomic validation, and CREATED shipment cancellation\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Added findByOrderId(orderId) method to query shipments by order\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — Added validation to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders\n5. `ApiError.kt` — Added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_IS_CANCELLED error codes\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Added 6 tests for cancel behaviour: active order without shipments, with CREATED shipments, already cancelled (idempotent), with CONFIRMED shipment (atomic rejection), non-existent order, and default ACTIVE status\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added 2 tests for shipment creation: rejection for CANCELLED order and baseline preservation for non-existent order\n\n**Tests:**\n- `test_newly_created_order_has_ACTIVE_status` — Verifies orders default to ACTIVE\n- `test_cancels_an_active_order_without_shipments` — Verifies cancellation transitions order to CANCELLED\n- `test_cancels_an_active_order_and_cancels_its_CREATED_shipments` — Verifies CREATED shipments are cancelled with order\n- `test_cancelling_an_already_cancelled_order_is_idempotent` — Verifies second cancel succeeds without changes\n- `test_cannot_cancel_order_with_a_CONFIRMED_shipment` — Verifies atomic rejection: order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n- `test_cannot_cancel_a_non_existent_order` — Verifies 404 for unknown orders\n- `test_rejects_shipment_creation_for_a_cancelled_order` — Verifies 409 when creating shipment for CANCELLED order\n- `test_creates_a_shipment_for_a_non_existent_order` — Verifies baseline behaviour preserved\n- Plus 13 existing tests all still pass\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ returned BUILD SUCCESS with 21 tests passing (10 OrderController + 7 Shipment + 3 Customer + 1 Application = 21), 0 failur